VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  The alpha_1 kill is NOT an artefact of the aether embedding.  Its killing piece -4(2-K_B)/(J_Y+1) is
  irreducible: independent of every free kinetic parameter, sign-definite whenever the MOND coupling is on, and
  zero exactly when MOND is off.  So alpha_1 = 0 is unreachable without a spin-1 ghost -- a structural lock, not a
  tuned number.  The same MOND-generating coupling kills the other two local preferred-frame embeddings through
  different health conditions (c_T for a curvature-coupled clock, a radial gradient instability for an
  acceleration-coupled khronon), both committed.  With the frame-free branch already dead on slip (and its
  disformal escape closed today on c_T), the LOCAL preferred-frame class is closed.
  DOOR A IS CLOSED FOR ALL LOCAL COMPLETIONS, conditional on locality (A2).  The only surviving door is the
  nonlocal spin-2 one (door B), which this theorem does not address and which is not door A.  Combined with the
  constraint-branch pincer (N_grav=2 <=> instantaneous <=> alpha_3=O(1)) and the frame-free slip kill, every
  local relativistic completion of the framework's exact kernel is now closed by a committed argument.

